What the handheld installs on the smart camera (an M5Stack UnitV, K210)
over USB-A and the Grove port, and where each part comes from.

catalyst-coprocessor.bin, firmware.version
  Catalyst Coprocessor: Catalyst Linux's own build of MaixPy (Sipeed's
  MicroPython for the K210) at commit d8901fd2272f000226f1c1037c1eb7c412b88e66
  (v0.6.3-2, the build M5Stack ships on the UnitV), trimmed to what the
  UnitV uses, with Catalyst's `catalyst` module (power, the speech front
  end) and frozen boot. Built by tools/unitv/firmware/build.sh in the
  Catalyst Linux source from the sources pinned and hashed in
  tools/unitv/firmware/versions.lock, with the changes in
  tools/unitv/firmware/patches.
  Source: https://github.com/sipeed/MaixPy-v1 and its submodules (Kendryte's
  standalone SDK, MicroPython, SPIFFS), at the commits versions.lock names.
  Licence: MIT (MicroPython, OpenMV, SPIFFS) and Apache-2.0 (Sipeed's and
  Kendryte's code); licences/MaixPy-LICENSE.md.

face.kmodel
  Sipeed's YOLOv2 face detector (facedetect.kmodel from
  machine_vision/models/face_model_at_0x300000.kfpkg), written to the
  K210's flash at 0x300000, where main.py loads it.
  Source: https://github.com/sipeed/MaixPy_scripts at
  8d7c5f98ba654d226f433d31718d852674cab08d.
  Licence: MIT; licences/MaixPy_scripts-LICENSE.

kws.kmodel, kws.json
  The keyword spotter for voice commands: a small CNN trained by Catalyst
  Linux (tools/unitv/speech) on Google's Speech Commands v0.02, compiled for
  the K210's KPU by Kendryte's nncase v0.2.0-beta4.
  Data licence: CC-BY-4.0; licences/speech-commands-ATTRIBUTION.

isp.bin
  The K210's flash-mode loader: kflash.py's ISP_PROG, loaded into the
  K210's SRAM to write its flash, never kept on the camera.
  Source: https://github.com/kendryte/kflash.py at
  5783d8d85e7397007a3ba1394a93d3f9f8ad982f.
  Licence: MIT; licences/kflash.py-LICENSE.

main.py
  Catalyst Linux's own program for the camera (tools/unitv/main.py in the
  Catalyst Linux source), written to the camera's /flash.
